# Under the hood, <any> means "anything with a value". <null>, naturally, doesn't fit this description. The current implementation of <any> is: #

<type> : <string><int8><int16><int32><int64><int128><int256><uint8><uint16><uint32><uint64><uint128><uint256><float16><float32><float64><float128><boolean><error>
-> <any> : <type><type[]>

# In older versions that didn't support generics, it was common to find: #

-> or <any> : (value <any><null>, else <any>) 's {
    | value <null> | {
        's -> else;
        's.leave();
    };

    -> value;
};
